{
  format: 1
  name: module-value-install-move-spellings
  suite: static
  spec: ["#modules", "§13.16", "§8.5"]
  note: '''
    §13.16 gives the move operator three lifecycle spellings, and all three must
    type at load rather than only at the transition that performs them:

    - "Install / override": `.modules[@id] <- unpack(@package)` — a fresh module
      value moved into a slot. The destination is written relative to the
      containing row, so this is also the spelling whose display path must
      interleave that row's key.
    - The bound form: `m <- unpack(@package)` then `.modules[@id] <- m`. §8.5
      makes `=` a copy and §13.16 makes `module` move-only, so `<-` is the ONLY
      way a module binds to a local at all — `m = unpack(@package)` is a load
      error.
    - "Move": `.modules[@to] <- @at`, relocating a module the host lent as a
      `module` parameter (§13.16 "Delegation"), which empties the source slot.

    An unambiguous destination is spelled either through the containing row
    (`.companies[@company].modules[@name]`) or rooted (`/modules[@name]`); both
    appear here so both resolve at load.
  '''

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.modinstall.spellings@1.0.0"
    $model: {
      modules: { $modules: {} }
      companies: {
        $key: "id"
        id: "text"
        modules: { $modules: {} }
      }
      $mut: {
        // §13.16 "Install / override".
        "provision({ company: text, name: text, package: blob })": [
          ".companies[@company].modules[@name] <- unpack(@package)"
        ]
        // The bound form: a module binds to a local only through `<-`.
        "provision_bound({ company: text, name: text, package: blob })": [
          "m <- unpack(@package)"
          ".companies[@company].modules[@name] <- m"
        ]
        // The package-root space, spelled unambiguously.
        "provision_root({ name: text, package: blob })": [
          "/modules[@name] <- unpack(@package)"
        ]
        // §13.16 "Move": relocate a module the host lent.
        "relocate({ company: text, to: text, at: module })": [
          ".companies[@company].modules[@to] <- @at"
        ]
      }
    }
    $data: { companies: { acme: {} } }
  }

  expect: { outcome: ok }
}
